// Title: DLL Sideloading Of ShellChromeAPI.DLL
// Sigma ID: ee4c5d06-3abc-48cc-8885-77f1c20f4451
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-12-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects processes loading the non-existent DLL "ShellChromeAPI". One known example is the
//   "DeviceEnroller" binary in combination with the "PhoneDeepLink" flag tries to load this DLL.
//   Adversaries can drop their own renamed DLL and execute it via DeviceEnroller.exe using this
//   parameter
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://mobile.twitter.com/0gtweet/status/1564131230941122561
//   - https://strontic.github.io/xcyclopedia/library/DeviceEnroller.exe-24BEF0D6B0ECED36BB41831759FDE18D.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_shell_chrome_api.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\ShellChromeAPI.dll"
